tickerbox talks to a TickerBox ESP32 device's REST API over HTTP. Target a device with --host, or register named devices with `tickerbox device add` and select one with --device or `tickerbox device use`. The device's REST API has no authentication; anything on its network can reach it.

Usage:
  tickerbox [command]

Examples:
  tickerbox device add desk http://tickerbox.local
  tickerbox status --device desk
  tickerbox --host http://192.168.1.42 wifi status

Available Commands:
  ap          Access point
  brightness  Set display brightness
  clock       Clock screen settings
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  config      Device configuration snapshot: export, import, diff
  device      Manage configured devices
  display     Display brightness / rotation / sleep
  doctor      Read-only health check
  fmp         Financial Modeling Prep API key, used to verify ticker symbols on add
  help        Help about any command
  ntp         NTP / time sync
  open        Open the device's web UI in the default browser
  profile     Named, device-agnostic device configurations
  reboot      Restart the device (alias for system restart)
  status      Aggregate dashboard
  system      System, status, maintenance
  ticker      Ticker / asset list
  time        Device wall-clock time
  tz          Time zones
  uptime      Show device uptime since last boot
  version     Print the CLI version
  watch       Re-run a read-only view on an interval until interrupted
  wifi        Wi-Fi station configuration

Flags:
  -d, --device string      named device from the config file
  -h, --help               help for tickerbox
      --host string        TickerBox base URL (default http://tickerbox.local, or $TICKERBOX_HOST)
  -j, --json               emit raw device JSON instead of a decoded table
      --retry int          retry an idempotent request this many times on a transient failure (default 2)
      --timeout duration   per-request timeout (default 10s)

Use "tickerbox [command] --help" for more information about a command.
